{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/pulls/239","id":4175128065,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSUkqqs7422YB","html_url":"https://github.com/the-sarge/cpace/pull/239","diff_url":"https://github.com/the-sarge/cpace/pull/239.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/the-sarge/cpace/pull/239.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/issues/239","number":239,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Prepare the v0.1.3 candidate contract (#231, #232)","user":{"login":"the-sarge","id":3312309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3312309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge","html_url":"https://github.com/the-sarge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Outcome\n\nThis PR combines issues #231 and #232: it adopts Go 1.26.5 as the repository toolchain, freezes `1f19e278112fa037890848ed6c086addeffdca4e` as the exact clean v0.1.3 candidate source, and publishes the pre-v1 migration and evidence-freshness contract.\n\nCloses #231.\nCloses #232.\n\nThe parent release tracker #229 remains open. Exact-candidate evidence begins in #233 and continues through #237; this PR does not claim production readiness.\n\n## Acceptance criteria — #231\n\n> - [ ] The repository pins Go 1.26.5 consistently for local and CI use without changing the supported Go language version unnecessarily.\n> - [ ] Documentation records why the security-release update is in v0.1.3 and marks earlier toolchain evidence as historical.\n> - [ ] Documentation identifies the Go 1.26.4 to 1.26.5 vector comparison and full exact-candidate evidence refresh as required follow-up gates.\n> - [ ] Documentation, unit, race, static-analysis, vulnerability, and policy checks appropriate to the toolchain change pass.\n> - [ ] No public API, wire, protocol, dependency, or package-profile change is introduced.\n\n## Acceptance criteria — #232\n\n> - [ ] The exact clean candidate commit is recorded after the PR #227 disposition and Go 1.26.5 update are settled.\n> - [ ] The admitted scope excludes Rapid, optional cleanup, new dependencies, new public API or behavior, ADR-0010 consideration, monorepo work, and cross-suite work.\n> - [ ] Migration guidance leads with the Config-to-Input change, exported Suite removal, and nil-safe Session.Close contract change.\n> - [ ] Additive lifecycle and peer-share error APIs are documented, and unchanged wire format and suite identity are explicit.\n> - [ ] Release posture states that v0.1.3 is not production-ready and that #29-#32 remain future production-readiness blockers rather than prerelease blockers.\n> - [ ] Any change after the freeze that affects security-relevant state is defined to restart the affected evidence lanes.\n\n## Review contract\n\nSupported input domain: every tracked Go module declaration in this repository and the release-facing documents changed by this PR. The authoritative representation owners are each module's `go.mod` for toolchain selection, `docs/v0.1.3-release-plan.md` for candidate scope, `docs/evidence-baseline.md` for evidence freshness, and `CHANGELOG.md` for migration guidance.\n\nGuarantee level: universal over the finite tracked module set and the named candidate-SHA references; canonical-subset over the repository release documents named above. The exact candidate source is the clean #231 commit, while the following #232 commit contains only release/process documentation.\n\nMaterial artifact classes: the Go toolchain directives are build/release configuration; the changelog is user-facing migration documentation; the release plan, checklist, evidence baseline, project plan, and reviewer handoff are process and traceability metadata. No runtime source or public API changes are included.\n\nContract ceilings and non-goals: no new dependency, API, observable behavior, wire/protocol, parser/framing, package-profile, fuzz-harness, Rapid, ADR-0010 proposal or consideration, monorepo, cpace-x25519, or cross-suite work. ADR-0010 and monorepo-plan files are absent from this branch. Exact-candidate dependency, SAST, fuzz, security/spec, vector, release-control, and publication evidence belongs to #233-#238.\n\nNamed regressions: all three module files must select Go 1.26.5 while retaining the Go 1.26 language line; the first three v0.1.3 changelog entries must cover Config-to-Input, Suite removal, and nil-safe Session.Close; every candidate reference must name `1f19e278112fa037890848ed6c086addeffdca4e`; required historical evidence must remain described as historical; no ADR-0010 or monorepo-plan artifact may enter the diff.\n\nTerminating evidence plan: one full `task check` on the exact final head; focused candidate-contract assertions and `git diff --check`; one fully briefed initial RAS review, verification only for independently accepted fix-now findings, and at most one replacement review after fixes; then the protected GitHub `Check`, `DCO`, `Dependency Gate`, and `SAST Gate` checks on the same exact head. Mutation budget is zero because this finite documentation/configuration slice adds no runtime enforcement guard. Operational repeat budget is one local full gate and one hosted run per required lane; platform budget is the local environment plus the required GitHub-hosted lanes; review-round budget is the initial review plus at most one replacement review.\n\nThis is the initial review contract. There are no settled RAS findings or linked review run IDs yet.\n\n## Local evidence so far\n\n- `task docs:check`\n- `task quick`\n- focused candidate-contract assertions\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe full exact-head certification and hosted checks are intentionally completed after the bounded review loop.\n","created_at":"2026-07-31T04:52:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T05:39:22Z","closed_at":"2026-07-31T05:39:20Z","merged_at":"2026-07-31T05:39:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"f310ba2fb8967081245b6092922f933c034d3db1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/pulls/239/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/pulls/239/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/issues/239/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-sarge/cpace/statuses/ff73e9ebcbdabfc949e8905caba526cec5057f38","head":{"label":"the-sarge:release/v0.1.3-231-232","ref":"release/v0.1.3-231-232","sha":"ff73e9ebcbdabfc949e8905caba526cec5057f38","user":{"login":"the-sarge","id":3312309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTIzMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3312309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge","html_url":"https://github.com/the-sarge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-sarge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.